    "summary": "Astra single-pass source repair. Personally visually read all 47 selected original pages: four questions, twenty-one final-key pages, and twenty-two explicitly scoped preliminary-key pages. Restored missing source derivations, final formulas, alternate part-a key/rubric and original maps. Preserved two whole original problems, IDs 13 and 14, and native source parts. No separate model checker.",
    "sourceGaps": [
      "Final key pages 6 and 14 have null PDF content streams and are blank in both Poppler and PyMuPDF; missing Eagles passages recovered from preliminary key pages 7–8 and 14.",
      "Final key page 15 contains broken-image placeholders. The intact corresponding maps are recovered from preliminary key page 25.",
      "Final Antipod part a) and its marking scheme are absent; preliminary page 24 supplies both, but uses 43° rather than the question’s 44°. No matching 44° worked answer was invented.",
      "Antipod part e) keys end at the symbolic flying-time expression without a numerical value."
    ],
    "sourceDiscrepancies": [
      "Eagles final question gives Earth–Sun distance 14.96×10^7 km, preliminary question 15×10^7 km; both keys substitute 15×10^7 km, radius 6380 km instead of 6370 km, and cos(45°21′) instead of the stated latitude 45°.",
      "Eagles B2 wording “on the plateau” is printed in the question but struck through in the final key’s repeated question. Original question retained.",
      "Antipod final question gives Moon distance 385000 km; preliminary question and both keys use 384400 km. The key’s printed magnitude sign inconsistency is retained.",
      "Antipod preliminary key prints 43° Nord and 43° Sud while both questions give 44° North. Its answer is explicitly attributed to that edition, not presented as a corrected final answer."
    ],
